cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PIGSTI, please cite this software (and the associated paper when
  available). Always record the exact release tag or commit SHA used for your run
  (see results/final/run_manifest.json).
title: "PIGSTI: a modular, reproducible pipeline for detecting species identity, pathogens, and microbes from animal palaeogenomic data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lhote
    given-names: Louis
    affiliation: "Trinity College Dublin"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LouisLhote/PIGSTI"
url: "https://github.com/LouisLhote/PIGSTI"
keywords:
  - ancient DNA
  - palaeogenomics
  - pathogen detection
  - pathogen authentication
  - host identification
  - Snakemake
  - metagenomics
  - KrakenUniq
  - HOPS
abstract: >-
  PIGSTI (Pathogen anImal Genome Sequence ToolkIt) is a Snakemake pipeline for
  screening and detecting pathogens in shotgun sequencing data from ancient animal
  remains. It performs competitive host species identification, host and mtDNA
  genome mapping, KrakenUniq-based metagenomic screening with Guellil E-value
  filtering (optional HOPS validation), pathogen reference mapping, and
  multi-criteria authentication, producing outputs suitable for population
  genetics and phylogenetic analyses.
